{
  "_comment": [
    "Clubs whose history is split across two spellings in the stored results,",
    "with the variants that should be read as one team.",
    "",
    "TYPED PAIRS ONLY. Everything a normaliser can settle on its own is",
    "settled in store.name_groups by the canonical key — `Chelsea FC` onto",
    "`Chelsea`, `AFC Ajax` onto `Ajax`, every accent variant. 288 folds come",
    "from there and need no line here. What lands in this file is the case no",
    "algorithm should attempt: one spelling ABBREVIATES a word the other",
    "spells out. `Man United` and `Manchester United` share no key, and",
    "loosening the key far enough to join them would also join Sunderland to",
    "Sheffield United. So the mapping is data rather than an algorithm, and",
    "every entry below was read off the store's own name list.",
    "",
    "Cause of the split: the results provider changed convention on",
    "2024-08-10, from terse trading names to full legal ones, and the store",
    "kept both. Before this file and the canonical fold, 22.2% of every row",
    "stored since that date was invisible to the spelling a hand-typed fixture",
    "resolves to — over 60% in ESP-L2 and POR-PL, 47% in ENG-PL. Chelsea,",
    "Ajax, Porto, Roma, Juventus and Valencia each lost their entire modern",
    "record, and the engine priced them on spring-2024 form.",
    "",
    "THE SAFETY TEST, applied to every pair here and to every automatic fold:",
    "a club plays at most one match a day, so two spellings that ever appear",
    "on the same date are different clubs and the fold is REFUSED. A wrong",
    "line in this file therefore fails closed rather than quietly joining two",
    "clubs' records. It is what keeps Paraguay's `Club Nacional` apart from",
    "Uruguay's `Nacional`, and Finland's `FC Inter` from Inter Milan, in the",
    "continental cups where both play.",
    "",
    "DELIBERATELY NOT MERGED — read once, so the next scan does not re-raise",
    "them:",
    "  reserve sides, a different team playing a different league — Malaga / Malaga B, Celta / Celta B, Sevilla / Sevilla B, Villarreal / Villarreal B, Sociedad / Sociedad B, Jong FC Twente / FC Twente",
    "  different clubs that share a word — Cove Rangers / Rangers, Club Brugge / Cercle Brugge, Sporting CP / Sporting Braga, Paris FC / Paris SG, Bastia / CA Bastia, FC Santa Coloma / UE Santa Coloma, FK Sarajevo / Željezničar Sarajevo, Hibernian / Hibernians, Partizan / FK Partizani, AC Milan / FK Milano, Athletic Club / Wigan Athletic, Arsenal / Arsenal Kyiv, Spartak / Spartak Moscow, Aris / Aris Limassol",
    "  same name, different city — the trap South America is full of — Estudiantes / Estudiantes Rio Cuarto, Independiente / Independiente del Valle, Independiente / Independiente Santa Fe, Nacional / Club Nacional, Botafogo / Botafogo-SP, Guarani / Guarani SP, Atlético San Luis / Club San Luis, Granada / Granada 74",
    "  a dissolved club and its successor, which share a city and a fanbase but not a record — Liaoning / Liaoning Tieren, Qingdao FC / Qingdao Hainiu, Shenzhen / Shenzhen Xinpengcheng, WSG Tirol / FC Wacker Tirol, AVS / Aves, Beveren / Waasland-Beveren"
  ],
